# Microsoft 365 MCP Integration

## Purpose

Provide agent access to approved Microsoft 365 resources through MCP.

## Supported Operations

* Search documents
* Read documents
* Search SharePoint sites
* Retrieve Teams content
* List files

## Authentication

Microsoft Entra ID authentication.

## Authorization

Users only access resources they already have permission to view.

## Error Handling

* Authentication failure
* Authorization failure
* Resource not found
* Timeout

## Logging

All MCP calls are logged according to organizational policy.


# Available MCP Tools

| Tool              | Purpose                        |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------ |
| search_documents  | Search Microsoft 365 documents |
| read_document     | Retrieve document content      |
| search_sharepoint | Search SharePoint repositories |
| list_files        | List available files           |
| search_teams      | Search Teams content           |

## Notes

All tools inherit Microsoft 365 permissions.

# MCP Integrations

## Microsoft 365 MCP

Use when:

* Searching SharePoint
* Reading documents
* Discovering runbooks
* Finding project artifacts

Do Not Use When:

* Data already exists in Fabric Lakehouse
* Data can be obtained through approved internal APIs
* High-volume ETL processing is required

Preferred Data Path

1. Fabric
2. Approved Internal APIs
3. Microsoft 365 MCP
4. Manual Upload


# MCP Error Handling

## Authentication Failure

Action:

* Reauthenticate user.
* Retry request.

## Authorization Failure

Action:

* Return access denied message.
* Do not bypass permissions.

## Resource Not Found

Action:

* Return resource identifier.
* Suggest search operation.

## Timeout

Action:

* Retry once.
* Return timeout status.

